 "copertura": {
  "numeri_totali": 599,
  "numeri_coperti": 535,
  "percentuale": 89.3,
  "frasi_con_numeri_non_coperti": 49,
  "elenco": [
   {
    "frase": "Introduction Cardarine, also known by the name of GW501516 (2-[2-methyl-4-[[4-methyl-2-[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]-1,3-thiazol-5-yl]methylsulfanyl]phenoxy]acetic acid), is a peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor del",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2",
     "4",
     "2",
     "4",
     "1"
    ],
    "n": 5
   },
   {
    "frase": "The PPAR-δ agents developed, including cardarine, are increasing the body’s capacity to use fat as a primary source of fuel as an alternative to glucose [2,3].",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2,3"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "The boost in fatty acid metabolism is gained based on the PPAR-δ receptor activation by the upregulation of fatty acid uptake and oxidation [4,5].",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "4,5"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Recent studies demonstrated that cardarine is efficient in the treatment of insulin resistance [6] and subepithelial fibrosis during asthma as well [7].",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "6",
     "7"
    ],
    "n": 2
   },
   {
    "frase": "Due to the fact that it boosts the body’s cardiovascular output, it gained rapid popularity among athletes and recreational users as a performance-enhancement drug [8,9]; nevertheless, its usage is prohibited by the Worl",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "8,9",
     "10"
    ],
    "n": 2
   },
   {
    "frase": "The polymorphism of active pharmaceutical ingredients represents their ability to be packed within the crystal structure in various patterns [13,14,15].",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "13,14"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "The formation of solid crystalline forms and multi-component molecular structures that contain at least two constituents are driven by noncovalent contacts such as hydrogen bonds, π···π stacking, and other van der Waals ",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "16,17"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Among the advantages and benefits of the solid forms, the following characteristics are worth mentioning: greater solubility, bioavailability, dissolution rate, melting point, and stability [18,19,20].",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "18,19"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "The stability of the polymorph and the 4,4′-bipyridine cocrystal was evaluated under specific temperature and relative humidity conditions.",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "4,4"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Materials and Methods ## 2.1.",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2.1"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "## 2.2.",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2.2"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "The collection of experimental data and their correction process for Lorentz, polarization, and adsorption effects were accomplished in the CrysAlis PRO program [21].",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "21"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "The structures were refined using Least Squares minimization by the SHELXL [24] refinement package.",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "24"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "All programs are implemented in the Olex2 package [25].",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "25"
    ],
    "n": 1
